// R1643 — BUG FIX: bugs.rtf #5 — study auto-plays prev word audio when no
// Lebanese audio available. Root cause not in speakSmart (R1607 covered that)
// but in repeatSpeak (Run #43). When user rates "Again", rate() fires
// repeatSpeak(currentCard.ar, 2, 700) — captures OLD card.ar by closure.
// Loop body awaits speak(text), then sleeps 700ms, then awaits speak(text)
// again. Meanwhile advanceStudy → showNextCard → speak(newCard.ar) starts.
// stopAllAudio bumps _speakGen, but repeatSpeak's outer loop is unaware —
// after the 700ms sleep it calls speak() with the OLD text, which plays the
// old card's audio over the new card's playback. If the new card has no
// Lebanese audio, the only audible output is the OLD card's repeat.
