// ===== R1700 — BUG FIX: speak() multi-word romanized lookup =====
// bugs.rtf #1 "sentence audio is often not Lebanese arabic". R1576 wraps
// speak() to convert single-word romanized → Arabic via __r1573Map. But it
// rejects multi-word inputs (`s.indexOf(' ') > -1 → reject`). Recent coaches
// (EHD R1698, QSH R1605, etc.) have multi-word entries like "mar mama",
// "kfar zayna", "nahr abu ali", "3id mar mama", "bayit jdid", "mar serkis"
// — all stored as keys in __r1573Map with their Arabic value, but the
// speak() wrap never looks them up. Result: clicking 🔊 on "mar mama" calls
// speak('mar mama') which falls through to speakSmart → segmentSentence
// chunks "mar"/"mama" → no audio → TTS pronounces ENGLISH letters.
// FIX: wrap speak() to also handle multi-word romanized inputs by checking
// for the whole phrase as a key in __r1573Map. Also handles ex-sentence
// keys stored by R1591/.../R1699 audio synth IIFEs.
